From 91c3af48462bf81049982d6337f06cb1265ffc2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy J Fontaine <tjfontaine@atxconsulting.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 19:50:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 39/40] bifrost: introduce TaskRef RAII for task lifetime
 safety

Wrap C-side get_task_struct/put_task_struct in a Rust RAII type so
attach paths can't leak or double-free task references on early
returns. Migrates every find_task_by_comm caller in attach.rs to
TaskRef::find, dropping the manual put_task_ref calls. slots.rs
pre-allocates MAX_PROBE_SLOTS (256) at module init so the spine
can't reallocate while uprobes fire on another CPU.

Closes goal items 4 (slot spine resize race) and 6 (task_struct
lifetime across C/Rust boundary).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
